    "available_at": "2026-11-03T17:36:09.004510+00:00",
    "body": "The latest Treasure Hunt clue has been released to subscribers. Credit: Adobe Stock\nPosted By: Northern Miner Staff November 3, 2026\nThe Northern Miner is excited to share that the latest Bonus Prize clue has just been emailed to all subscribers!\nAs we celebrate an incredible year of discovery, we’re taking a moment to look back at the treasure still waiting to be claimed.\nThe Great Canadian Treasure Hunt has pushed Canadians across the country to dig deeper, think smarter, and explore further than ever before. With an amazing journey behind us, the excitement is far from over; the adventure continues, the hunt remains wide open, and long hidden treasures sit waiting for discovery.\nWhether you’ve been following every twist and turn from day one or are just joining the adventure now, all of our exclusive subscriber content—available in both English and French—remains accessible to help you retrace your steps, review past clues, and stay hot on the trail.\nIf you’re a paid subscriber and need any assistance reviewing past updates or accessing your subscriber content, please reach out to us at treasure@northernminer.com . Our team is here to make sure you have everything you need to stay in the hunt.\nMore updates are on the way as the contest rolls forward. As always, keep digging.\nThis campaign is proudly presented with the support of industry sponsors including Agnico Eagle Mines, Sprott Money, EarthLabs, Iamgold, Kinross Gold, The World Gold Council, Alamos Gold, Ernst & Young, MINING.COM, CEO.CA and The Canadian Mining Journal.\nFor more information, including full contest rules, FAQs and updates, visit treasure.northernminer.com. Follow @northernminer (X/FB/YouTube) | @thenorthernminer (IG) | @mining (X) | @miningdotcom (IG/FB/YouTube) | @ceodotca (X/IG/FB/TikTok) | @ceocafilm (YouTube) for ongoing clues and community updates.\nPrint\nCOMMODITY: Gold\nREGION: Canada\nRepublish this article",
